.SH NAME
gmb-doc-check - Check documentation freshness and drift (CI gate)


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgmb doc check [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Audits all managed documents for drift and freshness without modifying any files.

.PP
With --check-external, a second pass verifies external http(s) links via
HEAD requests (internal reference checks never touch the network).
Unreachable hosts and network errors are skipped silently (offline-safe);
only completed HTTP 4xx/5xx responses are reported as failures.

.PP
Exit codes (plan Section 11):
  0  All documents are fresh (warnings allowed)
  1  Drift detected (one or more failures, including doc-lint asserts)
  2  Hard error (config or state could not be loaded)


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--check-external\fP[=false]
	Also verify external http(s) links via HEAD (network errors are skipped; HTTP 4xx/5xx fail)

.PP
\fB--doc\fP=""
	Only check the document with this ID

.PP
\fB--fix\fP[=false]
	Deterministically fix failing snippets (modifies files; use without --json in CI gate mode)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for check

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Emit machine-readable JSON output

.PP
\fB--tag\fP=""
	Only check documents with this tag

.PP
\fB--verify-snippets\fP[=false]
	Verify executable code snippets in managed docs


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--color\fP="auto"
	Color output mode: auto|always|never

.PP
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP=""
	Config file path (default is $HOME/.glassmarble.yaml)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging

.PP
\fB--dir\fP=""
	Target repository directory for analysis and queries

.PP
\fB--max-json-mb\fP=0
	Refuse to load or commit an AKG state file (akg.json) larger than this many MiB (0 = unlimited)

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	Suppress non-error output

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	Verbose output logging


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Check all docs
  gmb doc check

  # Machine-readable output for CI
  gmb doc check --json

  # Check a specific document
  gmb doc check --doc auth
.EE


